        ]
      },
      {
        "sha": "45ee7a55de9e4b43d711941cfb1c6b8fdf4c205f",
        "node_id": "MDY6Q29tbWl0MTY1NzU5OTIzOjQ1ZWU3YTU1ZGU5ZTRiNDNkNzExOTQxY2ZiMWM2YjhmZGY0YzIwNWY=",
        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "name": "Braden Napier",
            "email": "brady.napier@dashos.net",
            "date": "2018-10-24T17:13:58Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "Michał Pierzchała",
            "email": "thymikee@gmail.com",
            "date": "2018-10-24T17:13:58Z"
          },
          "message": "fix makeHot to not re-render unnecessarily (#491)\n\nThis will fix the `makeHot` so it doesn't force-rerender every tiny little change that happens when used with routers.  It does this by not building a brand new component on every call of the resulting function. \r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst HotView = makeHot(() => HomeView, 'Home');\r\nconsole.log(HotView() === HotView());\r\n```\r\n\r\n> Before the above would return false, therefore a re-render would be forced every time . `getScreen` is called by `react-navigation`\r\n\r\nNote that this will still cause problems when utilized as documented since\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconsole.log(makeHot(() => HomeView, 'Home')() !== makeHot(() => HomeView, 'Home')())\r\n```\r\n\r\nSolution there would likely to use a `Map` of some sort to identify when we should return the previously created component instead of creating a new one.  Since I couldn't be 100% of the effects of doing this type of change I decided to at least make it fixable in the meantime. \r\n\r\nSee #490",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "c29f50bdc0d0dc8fae77600fe0b56509590a1c2b",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/haul/git/trees/c29f50bdc0d0dc8fae77600fe0b56509590a1c2b"
          },
